  "durable_format": "Choose the typed deploy_generic_state e1 sidecar-family option attached to incumbent DeployState/Transaction. Existing receipt/intent/inverse e1 bytes and compatibility readers remain. Explicitly join deployment/receipt digest/generation/plan identity and pending/committed state. This is the existing transaction owner extended, not a second receipt engine. Do not encode absence as a fake digest or store untyped JSON inside prior_state_handle.",
  "operation_data": "Closed versioned host-readable semantics records explicit Present/Absent desired state, absent/retained/unavailable before-state, per-resource scope/path/literal key, source/provider/descriptor/semantics pins, stable canonical plan/grant subject, private blob refs, completed/uncertain progress and actual failure boundary. Replace Debug/ephemeral host identity as durable semantics digest; keep live grant issuer binding private/non-deserializable. Historical grant identity is audit data, never reusable permission.",
  "host_boundary": "Keep existing GenericHost apply compatibility surface; add closed host-library preparation/inspection for upgrade, cleanup, inverse, recovery, adoption and explicit receipt-scoped revocation with fresh exact operation/resource approval. Forward apply/upgrade/recovery requires current selected+enabled source and current principal/policy/root/control checks. Cleanup/inverse after source removal/revocation uses separately current control/root/protected authority and retained closed semantics only, never selected_current/native or package code. Unknown/corrupt/missing retained semantics is explicit unsupported/partial status, never guessed. Revoked forward effects refuse. No CLI/MCP/world/context-engine requirement.",
  "adoption_matrix": "Support explicit import/adoption into generic deployment from each relevant existing donor family: deployment (including legacy/C2/OpenCode where recorded closed resource grammar is representable), automatic package-skill, standalone skill. Support inverse/restoration of a recorded transfer back to its exact donor using retained donor-owned data and fresh authority. Arbitrary legacy-to-legacy or unrelated generic export is explicitly unsupported, not claimed as full3x3. No equal-byte inference or declaration-presence ownership. Each donor reads/validates/retires/restores its own family; lifecycle coordinates the transfer.",
  "coordination": "All current writers participating in supported adoption must join a common physical exclusion boundary via the incumbent SafeFS Project::lock primitive and canonical physical identity; preserve legacy family/deployment/destination leases. Stable global acquisition order must include donor/recipient/physical union, including pending operations, without cross-crate dependency cycles. Persist donor-visible transfer holds and recipient pending phases so a crash never permits two active owners or silently unowned residue; lock release alone does not erase durable ownership. If a narrow lower-level shared helper or public caller is necessary outside C3 named owners, ask exact file/symbol before edit, not create another lock engine.",
  "retention": "Before first destination effect persist exact needed before-images and desired bytes in bounded owner-controlled private blob storage through existing SafeFS/state owner; typed records contain references/digests/mode, not secret-bearing config bodies or executable code. Reuse existing content/state limits and explicit checked aggregate bounds; resource/retention refusal must be honest, not dropped effects. JSON/TOML inverse merges/restores only owned literal members, preserving current foreign neighbors. Whole-file restoration only with matching owned/current guarded state. Missing legacy before-images remain explicitly non-reversible; never reconstruct old bytes from a new descriptor. Restoring previously owned state must retain its true active ownership instead of being skipped merely as RolledBack.",
  "legacy_migration": "All three family readers/owners remain available. Legacy C2 data lacking retained operation/before-state is inspectable with explicit limits; migration/adoption requires explicit supplied closed semantics validated against exact old ownership and current grant. Do not invent historical before-images. Unknown new semantics refuses. No claim that old binary writers understand the new family; explicitly bind compatibility/feature-admission behavior rather than silently ignoring a present generic state.",
  "checks": "Bind actual new lifecycle/projection/wire families before compile, minimal representative positive/negative/crash/transfer cases covering full C3 obligations and supported donor matrix. Table-driven phase classes are enough; no exhaustive combinatorial crash matrix. Real typed family requires actual existing codegen and meaningful relevant format corpus checks. Preserve old generated Rust bodies; automatic generator-only source-list headers are allowed with exact body proof. Use actual impacted existing narrow cases; unchanged reuse is not new pass. Scoped rustfmt/XML+old-byte preservation. No broad suite/Lean/global facts/whole-project check from directory perimeter alone. If check-codegen needs integrated index, preserve original preintegration failure and run separately after Root integration, not fake a green run.",
  "full_task": "All original three steps, two positive/two negative cases, two acceptance criteria and safe stop remain. Do not finish only apply/cleanup helper; receipt migration plus isolated inverse/revocation and cross-family transfer evidence required. User prefers fast complete prototype, not old handoff/replay proof.",
